# The image serves the API only — content data lives in Supabase already
# (seeding runs from a dev machine), and the frontend deploys separately
# as a static site.
.git
.venv
node_modules
frontend
# Exclude the seed corpora but KEEP what the API reads from disk at runtime.
# Two things qualify, and BOTH were learned the same painful way — an
# exclusion here silently turns a feature off instead of failing a build:
#   data/gym         — Gym manifests. Excluding all of data/ made COPY
#                      data/gym a no-op and the Gym shipped empty.
#   *_frequency.tsv  — the collision guard. NLPBackend._collision_surfaces()
#                      reads data/<code>_frequency.tsv to decide whether a
#                      fold-only match landed on ANOTHER course word. Missing
#                      file -> except OSError -> empty set -> guard silently
#                      OFF, so `el` for `él` graded CORRECT_SLOPPY in
#                      production while 37 local tests passed. 8.6 MB.
# backend/tests/test_runtime_data_ships.py fails if this drifts again.
data/*
!data/gym
!data/*_frequency.tsv
#   data/*_readings.tsv — the ENTIRE reading layer for th, ar, he and fa. Each
#                      is looked up at request time from its table, so without
#                      them those readings are silently empty and nothing
#                      errors — indistinguishable from never having built it.
!data/*_readings.tsv
#   data/eval/calibrated.json — the nightly judge's gate: which (question,
#                      course) pairs may be sent to a model. Absent, it
#                      reads as EMPTY by design (a bad file must switch the
#                      judge off, never on), so with the admin switch ON the
#                      judge listed every pair "not calibrated", sent
#                      nothing, and every coverage row said calibrated:
#                      false. Only the json; the gold TSVs beside it are the
#                      calibration's evidence, read by hand, not by the API.
!data/eval/calibrated.json
# The nightly quality loop audits the corpus IN PRODUCTION, so the corpus has
# to be in the image. It was not, and the loop wrote 10,395 confident rows
# about files it could not see: every drill rule read 0 because data/grammar
# was absent, unclozable_rows read 0 because the sentence banks were, and the
# panel therefore showed 100% top-band coverage for all 27 courses. See
# CHECKS.md §44. ~41 MB, against an image that already carries 8.6 MB of
# frequency lists.
!data/grammar
!data/*_sentences.tsv
!data/sentences
!data/gloss_overrides.tsv
!data/quality
docs
scripts
# The migration FILES ship; nothing else under supabase/ does. They are not
# applied from the image (migrations are owner-applied) — they are read by
# backend/services/schema_check.py, which diffs them against the live
# database to say WHICH migration a 500 is waiting on. With the whole
# directory excluded that check found no expectations and reported `ok:
# true` from production for weeks while the database was behind: the
# diagnostic was blind exactly where it was needed.
supabase/*
!supabase/migrations
scratchpad
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.env
.env.*
